  # does not extend a lock hold, and no other `ws-add` waits on it. The
  # supervisor tick is the arm that makes this urgent, and it is enough on
  # its own.
  # Measured by the coordinator's review: 10 MB took 0.20 s
  # and 32 MB RSS, 100 MB took 39 s and 979 MB RSS — linear and unbounded.
  # It needs no exotic filesystem to reach: `ln -s ~/.cc-sessions/swap.log
  # pools/<p>` (or this branch's own documented alias in the other direction)
